1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,470
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,470 --> 00:00:05,030
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:05,030 --> 00:00:06,080
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,680 --> 00:00:08,910
I've laid brick for
forty-one years.

5
00:00:08,950 --> 00:00:10,350
Most of that on my knees,

6
00:00:10,350 --> 00:00:11,560
laying the bottom courses,

7
00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:12,780
one brick at a time.

8
00:00:13,110 --> 00:00:14,080
I had my right knee

9
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:15,640
replaced two years ago.

10
00:00:15,850 --> 00:00:17,950
It has hurt every day
since.

11
00:00:17,990 --> 00:00:19,100
Not surgery pain.

12
00:00:19,140 --> 00:00:20,220
I know what that felt
like,

13
00:00:20,220 --> 00:00:21,000
and it went away.

14
00:00:21,040 --> 00:00:21,950
This is different.

15
00:00:22,030 --> 00:00:22,560
Tight.

16
00:00:22,790 --> 00:00:23,280
Full.

17
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:24,120
Like a band around

18
00:00:24,120 --> 00:00:25,750
the joint that never
loosens.

19
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:26,780
And for two years I've

20
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:28,140
been told the same thing.

21
00:00:28,330 --> 00:00:29,260
Give it time.

22
00:00:29,630 --> 00:00:31,810
At six weeks it was
swelling,

23
00:00:31,810 --> 00:00:33,310
and swelling is normal.

24
00:00:33,510 --> 00:00:34,420
At three months,

25
00:00:34,420 --> 00:00:35,570
give it six.

26
00:00:35,790 --> 00:00:36,850
At six months,

27
00:00:36,850 --> 00:00:38,570
some knees take a full
year.

28
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:39,530
At a year,

29
00:00:39,530 --> 00:00:41,460
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

30
00:00:41,570 --> 00:00:42,650
And I didn't just wait.

31
00:00:42,690 --> 00:00:44,170
We went down the list.

32
00:00:44,260 --> 00:00:45,780
More physical therapy.

33
00:00:45,930 --> 00:00:47,010
Every session,

34
00:00:47,010 --> 00:00:48,640
every exercise at home.

35
00:00:48,860 --> 00:00:50,010
I got stronger.

36
00:00:50,050 --> 00:00:51,650
The tightness never moved.

37
00:00:51,830 --> 00:00:53,350
The pain pills helped,

38
00:00:53,350 --> 00:00:54,700
and that was the problem.

39
00:00:54,960 --> 00:00:56,990
I'm already on enough
every morning,

40
00:00:56,990 --> 00:00:58,110
and nobody could tell me

41
00:00:58,110 --> 00:00:59,160
when I'd get to stop.

42
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:01,150
Then a nerve block.

43
00:01:01,190 --> 00:01:03,290
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

44
00:01:03,360 --> 00:01:04,950
And after that, a second

45
00:01:04,950 --> 00:01:06,210
operation to go back

46
00:01:06,210 --> 00:01:07,610
in and do it over.

47
00:01:07,690 --> 00:01:08,810
I said no.

48
00:01:08,850 --> 00:01:10,280
Every morning I climbed
out

49
00:01:10,280 --> 00:01:11,390
of the truck at the job

50
00:01:11,390 --> 00:01:12,460
and my knee felt like

51
00:01:12,460 --> 00:01:14,590
a band was wrapped around
it,

52
00:01:14,590 --> 00:01:16,920
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

53
00:01:17,170 --> 00:01:18,510
Every morning I took
something

54
00:01:18,510 --> 00:01:20,290
for it and picked up my
trowel.

55
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:22,520
Couldn't kneel to lay a
bottom course,

56
00:01:22,520 --> 00:01:24,150
couldn't climb the
scaffold without

57
00:01:24,150 --> 00:01:25,820
stopping on every landing,

58
00:01:25,820 --> 00:01:27,310
couldn't carry a load of
brick up

59
00:01:27,310 --> 00:01:29,680
the ramp without favoring
that leg.

60
00:01:29,820 --> 00:01:31,530
The young guys on my crew
started

61
00:01:31,530 --> 00:01:33,590
laying my low courses for
me.

62
00:01:33,750 --> 00:01:35,320
A bricklayer who can't get
down

63
00:01:35,320 --> 00:01:36,780
on his knees is a
bricklayer

64
00:01:36,780 --> 00:01:37,910
running out of time.

65
00:01:38,420 --> 00:01:39,580
It woke me at night,

66
00:01:39,580 --> 00:01:41,570
and it turned ordinary
things,

67
00:01:41,570 --> 00:01:42,820
like getting in the truck

68
00:01:42,820 --> 00:01:44,250
or up off a bucket,

69
00:01:44,250 --> 00:01:45,390
into a decision.

70
00:01:45,570 --> 00:01:46,810
After a long and serious

71
00:01:46,810 --> 00:01:48,170
talk with my wife,

72
00:01:48,170 --> 00:01:49,890
I went back in one more
time.

73
00:01:50,050 --> 00:01:51,100
That was the fourth set

74
00:01:51,100 --> 00:01:52,580
of X-rays on this knee.

75
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:54,460
And like the three before
it,

76
00:01:54,460 --> 00:01:56,850
the answer was everything
looks great.

77
00:01:57,020 --> 00:01:59,270
No loosening, no
infection,

78
00:01:59,270 --> 00:02:00,290
nothing wrong.

79
00:02:00,550 --> 00:02:01,700
Only this time

80
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:02,970
there was no new number.

81
00:02:03,350 --> 00:02:05,910
Nobody said give it
another six months.

82
00:02:05,950 --> 00:02:07,600
There was nothing left to
give it.

83
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:08,500
I sat in the parking

84
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:09,390
lot for a while.

85
00:02:09,430 --> 00:02:10,410
Okay, I thought.

86
00:02:10,540 --> 00:02:11,790
Then explain this.

87
00:02:12,050 --> 00:02:14,150
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

88
00:02:14,150 --> 00:02:15,600
I hit my breaking point.

89
00:02:15,920 --> 00:02:17,970
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

90
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:20,080
Everyone in the house was
asleep

91
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:21,810
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

92
00:02:21,810 --> 00:02:22,930
with my leg up,

93
00:02:22,930 --> 00:02:24,500
trying to find any angle

94
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:25,670
where it didn't feel like

95
00:02:25,670 --> 00:02:27,620
something was wrapped
around my knee

96
00:02:27,620 --> 00:02:28,490
and tightening.

97
00:02:28,820 --> 00:02:29,720
I had a wall

98
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:30,850
to start at seven.

99
00:02:31,230 --> 00:02:33,540
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

100
00:02:33,580 --> 00:02:35,170
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

101
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:36,590
And I just thought,

102
00:02:36,590 --> 00:02:38,440
is this really how it
ends?

103
00:02:38,520 --> 00:02:39,540
Forty-one years,

104
00:02:39,540 --> 00:02:40,970
and I hang up the trowel

105
00:02:40,970 --> 00:02:42,200
because of a knee that
looks

106
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:43,620
great on an X-ray?

107
00:02:43,750 --> 00:02:45,600
So I made myself a
promise.

108
00:02:45,740 --> 00:02:46,650
I wouldn't go a day

109
00:02:46,650 --> 00:02:48,080
without looking for an
answer.

110
00:02:48,630 --> 00:02:50,000
And when I found one,

111
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,180
I'd share it with everyone

112
00:02:51,180 --> 00:02:52,480
going through the same
thing.

113
00:02:52,780 --> 00:02:54,520
So I got my laptop out

114
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:55,420
and went looking.

115
00:02:55,460 --> 00:02:56,660
Not for a product.

116
00:02:56,740 --> 00:02:58,030
For an explanation.

117
00:02:58,230 --> 00:02:59,630
Mayo Clinic forums,

118
00:02:59,630 --> 00:03:01,720
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

119
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:03,450
doctor videos,

120
00:03:03,450 --> 00:03:04,940
medical animations.

121
00:03:05,110 --> 00:03:05,980
And that's when I found

122
00:03:05,980 --> 00:03:07,140
a video from a physical

123
00:03:07,140 --> 00:03:09,870
therapist named Dr. Steven
Salinger,

124
00:03:09,870 --> 00:03:11,070
whose own wife had been

125
00:03:11,070 --> 00:03:12,510
through exactly this.

126
00:03:12,550 --> 00:03:14,760
But before I say anything
else,

127
00:03:14,760 --> 00:03:16,230
I want to be straight with
you.

128
00:03:16,460 --> 00:03:18,490
You've already had
something work fast.

129
00:03:18,530 --> 00:03:19,280
The ice.

130
00:03:19,320 --> 00:03:20,710
The first week of a new
pill.

131
00:03:20,750 --> 00:03:22,410
The good day after a
session.

132
00:03:22,640 --> 00:03:23,650
Then it wore off.

133
00:03:23,690 --> 00:03:25,710
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

134
00:03:25,890 --> 00:03:27,630
Fast relief isn't relief.

135
00:03:27,690 --> 00:03:28,660
It's a preview.

136
00:03:28,970 --> 00:03:29,910
So I'm not going to tell

137
00:03:29,910 --> 00:03:31,260
you this works fast.

138
00:03:31,300 --> 00:03:32,160
It doesn't.

139
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:34,120
But if you're willing to
be patient,

140
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:35,010
and to look at what's

141
00:03:35,010 --> 00:03:36,860
going on around your new
knee

142
00:03:36,860 --> 00:03:38,430
instead of inside it,
there

143
00:03:38,430 --> 00:03:40,790
is a real reason it still
hurts.

144
00:03:40,930 --> 00:03:42,600
And something you can do
about it.

145
00:03:42,750 --> 00:03:44,440
Let me explain what he
said,

146
00:03:44,440 --> 00:03:45,830
because this is what
changed

147
00:03:45,830 --> 00:03:46,870
everything for me.

148
00:03:46,910 --> 00:03:48,770
He started with the
basics.

149
00:03:48,810 --> 00:03:50,360
A knee replacement takes
out

150
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:52,040
the worn joint surfaces

151
00:03:52,040 --> 00:03:53,860
and puts in metal and
plastic.

152
00:03:54,080 --> 00:03:56,030
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

153
00:03:56,030 --> 00:03:57,740
you had before the
operation.

154
00:03:58,010 --> 00:03:59,640
That part I already knew.

155
00:03:59,980 --> 00:04:01,870
But then he explained
something

156
00:04:01,870 --> 00:04:03,260
nobody had ever told me.

157
00:04:03,300 --> 00:04:04,270
He said,

158
00:04:04,270 --> 00:04:05,580
think about a swollen foot

159
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:06,650
inside a shoe.

160
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:08,280
The shoe didn't shrink.

161
00:04:08,470 --> 00:04:10,740
Your foot is taking up
more room,

162
00:04:10,740 --> 00:04:12,310
so everything feels
cramped

163
00:04:12,310 --> 00:04:13,950
and tight and squeezed.

164
00:04:14,270 --> 00:04:15,220
Your new knee sits

165
00:04:15,220 --> 00:04:16,730
in a limited space with
living

166
00:04:16,730 --> 00:04:18,440
tissue packed all around
it.

167
00:04:18,610 --> 00:04:20,100
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

168
00:04:20,100 --> 00:04:21,740
had to work through that
tissue.

169
00:04:21,880 --> 00:04:24,310
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

170
00:04:24,660 --> 00:04:26,360
At first that's normal.

171
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:27,960
But in some people

172
00:04:27,960 --> 00:04:29,530
that swelling can stay
switched

173
00:04:29,530 --> 00:04:31,320
on far longer than
expected.

174
00:04:31,580 --> 00:04:33,250
And swollen tissue takes
up more

175
00:04:33,250 --> 00:04:35,030
room than calm tissue
does.

176
00:04:35,130 --> 00:04:36,680
So when you bend,

177
00:04:36,680 --> 00:04:38,390
that tissue gets
compressed.

178
00:04:38,430 --> 00:04:39,660
When you straighten,

179
00:04:39,660 --> 00:04:40,960
it gets pulled tight.

180
00:04:41,020 --> 00:04:42,190
That's the band.

181
00:04:42,260 --> 00:04:44,450
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

182
00:04:44,490 --> 00:04:45,370
And you start being

183
00:04:45,370 --> 00:04:46,150
the one who says,

184
00:04:46,150 --> 00:04:46,920
you go ahead.

185
00:04:46,960 --> 00:04:47,990
I'll stay here.

186
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:49,710
And that's exactly why so
much

187
00:04:49,710 --> 00:04:51,350
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

188
00:04:51,680 --> 00:04:53,560
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

189
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:54,510
around the knee.

190
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:55,470
Worth doing,

191
00:04:55,470 --> 00:04:56,360
and I'd done it.

192
00:04:56,580 --> 00:04:57,760
It does nothing about
tissue

193
00:04:57,760 --> 00:04:58,900
taking up room.

194
00:04:58,960 --> 00:05:00,010
A nerve block quiets

195
00:05:00,010 --> 00:05:01,710
the nerve carrying the
signal.

196
00:05:01,820 --> 00:05:03,670
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

197
00:05:04,170 --> 00:05:05,580
But when that irritated
tissue

198
00:05:05,580 --> 00:05:07,230
finally calms down,

199
00:05:07,230 --> 00:05:08,560
it holds less fluid,

200
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:09,920
and it takes up less room.

201
00:05:10,170 --> 00:05:11,480
Less room taken up means

202
00:05:11,480 --> 00:05:13,310
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

203
00:05:13,580 --> 00:05:15,570
That's what takes the
pressure off.

204
00:05:15,860 --> 00:05:17,350
After two years of this,

205
00:05:17,350 --> 00:05:18,930
it finally made sense.

206
00:05:19,270 --> 00:05:21,180
The problem was never the
new knee.

207
00:05:21,310 --> 00:05:23,220
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

208
00:05:23,560 --> 00:05:25,070
He calls it the squeeze.

209
00:05:25,150 --> 00:05:27,580
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

210
00:05:27,860 --> 00:05:29,310
I'd bought gel

211
00:05:29,310 --> 00:05:30,470
knee pads,

212
00:05:30,470 --> 00:05:32,220
a foam kneeling board,

213
00:05:32,220 --> 00:05:34,710
compression braces,
creams,

214
00:05:34,710 --> 00:05:36,510
half of Amazon really,

215
00:05:36,510 --> 00:05:37,960
and all any of it gave

216
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:39,350
me was an hour.

217
00:05:39,530 --> 00:05:40,420
I even looked at going

218
00:05:40,420 --> 00:05:42,150
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

219
00:05:42,320 --> 00:05:44,490
But at $200 a session

220
00:05:44,490 --> 00:05:46,240
with nothing covered by
insurance,

221
00:05:46,240 --> 00:05:47,900
that was a quick no.

222
00:05:48,310 --> 00:05:49,950
Then one night I went back

223
00:05:49,950 --> 00:05:51,540
to that knee replacement
group

224
00:05:51,540 --> 00:05:52,720
and actually read it.

225
00:05:53,060 --> 00:05:54,320
Thousands of people,

226
00:05:54,320 --> 00:05:55,980
years out from surgery,

227
00:05:55,980 --> 00:05:58,420
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

228
00:05:58,420 --> 00:05:59,830
nobody could explain.

229
00:05:59,940 --> 00:06:01,770
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

230
00:06:01,770 --> 00:06:03,840
the same thing kept coming
up.

231
00:06:04,180 --> 00:06:05,800
This one device,

232
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:07,040
and people saying

233
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:07,950
it was the first thing

234
00:06:07,950 --> 00:06:09,090
that made a difference.

235
00:06:09,130 --> 00:06:11,340
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

236
00:06:11,340 --> 00:06:12,920
alright, here it comes,

237
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:14,310
he's selling me something,

238
00:06:14,310 --> 00:06:16,120
let me shut that down
right now.

239
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:18,140
I'm only here because I
made myself

240
00:06:18,140 --> 00:06:20,260
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

241
00:06:20,260 --> 00:06:21,290
that if I ever found

242
00:06:21,290 --> 00:06:22,410
something that helped,

243
00:06:22,410 --> 00:06:23,340
I'd say so.

244
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:25,310
It's called the KenRelief
Red

245
00:06:25,310 --> 00:06:26,580
Light Therapy Wrap.

246
00:06:26,650 --> 00:06:28,500
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

247
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:30,780
It looked like the cheap
knee sleeves

248
00:06:30,780 --> 00:06:33,330
off Amazon that did
nothing for me.

249
00:06:33,650 --> 00:06:35,950
But I went to their
website anyway,

250
00:06:35,950 --> 00:06:36,950
just to see what all

251
00:06:36,950 --> 00:06:38,100
the fuss was about.

252
00:06:38,280 --> 00:06:40,410
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

253
00:06:40,410 --> 00:06:43,200
charge $200 a session for,

254
00:06:43,200 --> 00:06:46,170
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

255
00:06:46,170 --> 00:06:47,230
in a wrap you plug

256
00:06:47,230 --> 00:06:48,690
into the wall at home.

257
00:06:49,090 --> 00:06:50,770
Two hundred and forty
lights.

258
00:06:50,880 --> 00:06:52,920
Red at 660 nanometers

259
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:55,230
and near-infrared at 850,

260
00:06:55,230 --> 00:06:57,390
run together for the
strongest effect.

261
00:06:57,590 --> 00:06:59,290
Four strength levels.

262
00:06:59,500 --> 00:07:01,520
A five to thirty minute
timer.

263
00:07:01,940 --> 00:07:03,560
Then I saw the guarantee.

264
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:05,000
Ninety days.

265
00:07:05,190 --> 00:07:07,640
Results or your money
back,

266
00:07:07,640 --> 00:07:08,950
no questions,

267
00:07:08,950 --> 00:07:10,400
no store credit,

268
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:12,460
and you don't even send it
back.

269
00:07:12,500 --> 00:07:14,830
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

270
00:07:14,830 --> 00:07:16,230
days to change my mind.

271
00:07:16,270 --> 00:07:17,570
There wasn't much to lose,

272
00:07:17,570 --> 00:07:18,530
so I ordered it.

273
00:07:18,570 --> 00:07:19,800
Two of them, actually.

274
00:07:20,030 --> 00:07:22,240
Only the right knee was
replaced,

275
00:07:22,240 --> 00:07:24,350
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

276
00:07:24,350 --> 00:07:25,620
and I'd done it on every

277
00:07:25,620 --> 00:07:27,300
job for two years.

278
00:07:27,630 --> 00:07:30,190
The left one was carrying
the difference.

279
00:07:30,380 --> 00:07:30,950
When it came,

280
00:07:30,950 --> 00:07:33,020
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

281
00:07:33,020 --> 00:07:34,400
because I'd been let down
too

282
00:07:34,400 --> 00:07:36,000
many times to get excited.

283
00:07:36,260 --> 00:07:37,650
What I felt was warmth.

284
00:07:37,690 --> 00:07:39,690
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

285
00:07:39,810 --> 00:07:40,730
More like it was coming

286
00:07:40,730 --> 00:07:42,080
from inside the knee

287
00:07:42,080 --> 00:07:43,330
and spreading around it.

288
00:07:43,450 --> 00:07:44,520
And that was it.

289
00:07:44,750 --> 00:07:46,510
That was the whole
experience.

290
00:07:46,620 --> 00:07:47,860
When I took it off,

291
00:07:47,860 --> 00:07:48,820
I'll be honest,

292
00:07:48,820 --> 00:07:50,590
nothing dramatic had
happened.

293
00:07:50,670 --> 00:07:52,180
And after what that video
said,

294
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:54,490
that's exactly what I
expected.

295
00:07:54,740 --> 00:07:55,780
What was different

296
00:07:55,780 --> 00:07:56,610
was that for the first

297
00:07:56,610 --> 00:07:57,940
time in two years

298
00:07:57,940 --> 00:07:59,310
I'd done something for my
knee

299
00:07:59,310 --> 00:08:00,300
instead of to it.

300
00:08:00,840 --> 00:08:01,870
Twenty minutes,

301
00:08:01,870 --> 00:08:02,990
in my own chair,

302
00:08:02,990 --> 00:08:03,930
after work.

303
00:08:04,090 --> 00:08:05,500
No drive, no copay.

304
00:08:05,540 --> 00:08:07,040
They say twenty minutes.

305
00:08:07,160 --> 00:08:08,250
I did thirty,

306
00:08:08,250 --> 00:08:09,360
twice a day,

307
00:08:09,360 --> 00:08:11,330
lowest setting that first
week.

308
00:08:11,620 --> 00:08:13,520
Once before the truck in
the morning,

309
00:08:13,520 --> 00:08:14,540
once after supper.

310
00:08:14,580 --> 00:08:15,710
The first week,

311
00:08:15,710 --> 00:08:16,460
I couldn't have told

312
00:08:16,460 --> 00:08:17,780
you if anything was
happening.

313
00:08:18,020 --> 00:08:18,940
I tried not to get

314
00:08:18,940 --> 00:08:19,860
my hopes up.

315
00:08:20,120 --> 00:08:20,800
I'd had things help

316
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:22,100
for a week and then stop.

317
00:08:22,230 --> 00:08:23,560
But somewhere in the
second week

318
00:08:23,560 --> 00:08:24,560
I noticed I'd come down

319
00:08:24,560 --> 00:08:26,380
the stairs without holding
the rail.

320
00:08:26,910 --> 00:08:28,290
I hadn't decided to.

321
00:08:28,330 --> 00:08:29,470
I just did it,

322
00:08:29,470 --> 00:08:31,190
then stopped halfway down

323
00:08:31,190 --> 00:08:32,460
because I realized.

324
00:08:32,620 --> 00:08:34,280
By the end of the fourth
week

325
00:08:34,280 --> 00:08:35,360
I'd slept through the
night

326
00:08:35,360 --> 00:08:36,600
four times running.

327
00:08:36,960 --> 00:08:38,500
I stood at the counter and
finished

328
00:08:38,500 --> 00:08:40,650
making dinner without
looking for the stool.

329
00:08:40,940 --> 00:08:42,470
None of that is dramatic.

330
00:08:42,660 --> 00:08:43,520
All of it was gone

331
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:44,580
for two years.

332
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:46,220
A few weeks later

333
00:08:46,220 --> 00:08:47,130
my wife asked if I

334
00:08:47,130 --> 00:08:48,270
wanted to walk the long

335
00:08:48,270 --> 00:08:49,490
way around the block.

336
00:08:49,620 --> 00:08:50,500
And for the first time

337
00:08:50,500 --> 00:08:51,200
in two years,

338
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:52,410
I said yes.

339
00:08:52,770 --> 00:08:54,370
I wanted to understand
why,

340
00:08:54,370 --> 00:08:55,730
so I read the whole thing.

341
00:08:55,950 --> 00:08:57,630
It comes down to four
steps.

342
00:08:57,840 --> 00:08:58,410
One.

343
00:08:58,690 --> 00:09:00,480
The tissue around a new
knee can

344
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:03,530
stay inflamed long after
surgery is over.

345
00:09:03,980 --> 00:09:04,610
Two.

346
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:07,170
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

347
00:09:07,170 --> 00:09:08,090
so it takes up more

348
00:09:08,090 --> 00:09:09,500
room than it should.

349
00:09:09,750 --> 00:09:10,430
Three.

350
00:09:10,500 --> 00:09:12,340
There's only so much room
in there.

351
00:09:12,380 --> 00:09:13,960
Bending compresses it.

352
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:15,730
Straightening pulls it
tight.

353
00:09:15,850 --> 00:09:17,130
That's the squeeze.

354
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:18,790
Four.

355
00:09:19,170 --> 00:09:20,800
Red and near-infrared
light have been

356
00:09:20,800 --> 00:09:23,200
studied for calming that
inflammation,

357
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:24,550
so the swelling and the
pressure

358
00:09:24,550 --> 00:09:25,850
can come down with it.

359
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:27,830
In a randomized trial,

360
00:09:27,830 --> 00:09:29,450
patients given light
therapy after

361
00:09:29,450 --> 00:09:31,890
a knee replacement had
less pain,

362
00:09:31,890 --> 00:09:33,590
less swelling and better
early

363
00:09:33,590 --> 00:09:35,210
movement than those who
weren't.

364
00:09:35,750 --> 00:09:38,530
A 2025 review said the
same,

365
00:09:38,530 --> 00:09:39,770
and was clear the evidence

366
00:09:39,770 --> 00:09:40,860
is still limited.

367
00:09:41,110 --> 00:09:42,850
I probably sound like a
broken record

368
00:09:42,850 --> 00:09:44,420
to my family and my crew.

369
00:09:44,900 --> 00:09:46,760
But after two years of
doing everything

370
00:09:46,760 --> 00:09:48,880
I was told and getting
nowhere,

371
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:50,390
you have no idea what it's

372
00:09:50,390 --> 00:09:51,930
like to sleep through the
night,

373
00:09:51,930 --> 00:09:53,410
say yes to the walk,

374
00:09:53,410 --> 00:09:54,760
and get my life back.

375
00:09:54,920 --> 00:09:56,170
So take it from me.

376
00:09:56,620 --> 00:09:58,180
Don't spend another year
waiting

377
00:09:58,180 --> 00:09:59,180
for it to settle.

378
00:09:59,480 --> 00:10:01,300
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

379
00:10:01,550 --> 00:10:02,940
More than ten thousand
people

380
00:10:02,940 --> 00:10:04,120
with pain after a knee

381
00:10:04,120 --> 00:10:06,140
replacement have already
tried this.

382
00:10:06,350 --> 00:10:08,040
Some had it worse than I
did.

383
00:10:08,210 --> 00:10:09,640
You can get the KenRelief

384
00:10:09,640 --> 00:10:11,100
wrap from their website,

385
00:10:11,100 --> 00:10:12,620
